Contributing to Nexus SaaS Platform

First of all, thank you for your interest in contributing to Nexus SaaS Platform. We welcome contributions from developers, designers, technical writers, testers, and community members.

Our goal is to build a secure, scalable, AI-powered SaaS platform that follows modern engineering practices.

---

Code of Conduct

By participating in this project, you agree to:

- Be respectful and professional.
- Welcome constructive feedback.
- Help create an inclusive community.
- Avoid harassment or abusive behavior.
- Respect project maintainers and contributors.

---

Ways to Contribute

You can contribute by:

- Fixing bugs
- Adding new features
- Improving documentation
- Optimizing performance
- Reporting security issues
- Writing tests
- Improving UI/UX
- Reviewing pull requests

---

Development Workflow

1. Fork the repository.
2. Clone your fork locally.
3. Create a feature branch.
4. Make your changes.
5. Test your changes.
6. Commit using meaningful commit messages.
7. Push your branch.
8. Open a Pull Request.

---

Branch Naming

Use descriptive branch names:

feature/user-dashboard
feature/ai-chat
fix/login-bug
docs/api-update
refactor/database-layer

---

Commit Message Convention

Recommended format:

feat: add AI image generator

fix: resolve login issue

docs: update README

refactor: optimize API routes

test: add authentication tests

chore: update dependencies

---

Coding Standards

- Use TypeScript where possible.
- Write clean, readable code.
- Keep functions small and focused.
- Add comments only where necessary.
- Remove unused code before submitting.

---

Pull Request Checklist

Before opening a Pull Request:

- Code builds successfully.
- No linting errors.
- Tests pass.
- Documentation updated if needed.
- No sensitive information committed.
- Commit history is clean.

---

Issue Reporting

When reporting an issue, include:

- Operating System
- Browser (if applicable)
- Steps to reproduce
- Expected behavior
- Actual behavior
- Screenshots (if available)
- Error logs

---

Feature Requests

Please include:

- Problem statement
- Proposed solution
- Alternative approaches
- Expected benefits
- Example use case

---

Security

Do not disclose security vulnerabilities publicly.

Report security issues privately to the project maintainers before creating a public issue.

---

Documentation

Documentation improvements are always welcome.

You can help by:

- Fixing grammar
- Improving examples
- Adding tutorials
- Updating outdated sections

---

Testing

Before submitting code:

- Run unit tests
- Verify manual testing
- Ensure existing features continue working
- Test on supported environments when applicable

---

Review Process

Every Pull Request will be reviewed for:

- Code quality
- Maintainability
- Security
- Performance
- Documentation
- Compatibility

Maintainers may request changes before merging.

---

License

By contributing to this project, you agree that your contributions will be licensed under the project's license.

---

Thank You

Thank you for helping build Nexus SaaS Platform.

Your contributions make the project better for everyone.